# EVERY fixture here must be ENUMERATED on the out-of-profile path, never
# silently dropped and never merely counted -- a dropped axiom is an incoherence
# the reasoner subsequently cannot see. Each yields non-empty coverage.omitted,
# so the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2), never coherent.
# #
# Functional, inverse-functional, symmetric, asymmetric, irreflexive, reflexive.
# Note TransitiveObjectProperty is NOT here -- it is in v0, desugaring to r o r subseteq r.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix swrl: <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:f a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty .
:g a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:InverseFunctionalProperty .
:h a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:SymmetricProperty .
:i a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:AsymmetricProperty .
:j a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:IrreflexiveProperty .
:k a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:ReflexiveProperty .
